<title>CANADA: Canada union okay Northern Telecom deal.</title>
<headline>Canada union okay Northern Telecom deal.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Autoworkers union said on Thursday it voted in favor of a new three-year collective agreement with Northern Telecom Ltd.</p>
<p>The union said the agreement offers workers at the Brampton, Ontario, plant which it said has been hit by a number of layoff notices.</p>
<p>Hourly workers at Nortel's Brampton and Belleville, Ontario, plants voted 95.6 percent in favor of the deal. Salaried employees voted 93.1 percent for the agreement and skilled trades gave the deal 85.2 percent approval.  </p>
<p>The union said the contract provides wage and cost-of-living allowance improvements, benefit and major pension improvements as well as income security.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
